 ee-arts-celebration-downtown-sf/\nVenue: it all started. Join DVAN on Sund
 ay\, September 27 for the Warfield Commons Grand\nPrice: Free\nCategories:
  free\nSource: funcheap/san-francisco\n\nWarfield Commons celebrates its g
 rand opening in downtown San Francisco with a ribbon-cutting ceremony\, mu
 sic performances\, art activations\, local food vendors\, building tours\,
  and activities. Third-floor programming includes storytime\, poetry readi
 ngs\, office hours with Diasporic Vietnamese Artists Network staff\, child
 ren’s puppet shows\, and Well-Crafted activities. Third Floor Schedule 1
 2:30–4:30 PM – Well-Crafted Activities + Office Hours with DVAN Staff 
 1:00 PM – Tito Ramon’s Pop-Up Puppet Show 1:15 PM – DVAN Storytime w
 ith Minnie Phan\, Thien Pham & Thi Bui 2:00 PM – Music performance by Th
 e OSADA 3 3:00 PM – Tito Ramon’s Pop-Up Puppet Show 3:15 PM – DVAN P
 oetry Reading with Carolyn Ho\, Jean-Baptiste Phou\, Trinh Le\, Danny Thie
 n Le & Forrest Nguyen 4:00 PM – Music performance by Tori Roze and the H
 ot Mess Original Event Description: _DVAN has found a new home at @warfiel
 dcommons in the heart of downtown San Francisco! 🏠✨ We are proud to b
 e part of this vibrant hub for arts and media — and put down roots in th
 e city where it all started. Join DVAN on Sunday\, September 27 for the Wa
 rfield Commons Grand Opening hosted by @castsf\, @kalwpublicmedia\, @tlcbd
 \, and @marketstreetarts. Thi
LOCATION:it all started. Join DVAN on Sunday\, September 27 for the Warfie
 ld Commons Grand
